an>sph_bessel</span><span>sph_besself</span><span>sph_bessell</span></span></a></div><div><span class=\"t-lines\"><span><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx17\">(C++17)</span></span><span><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx17\">(C++17)</span></span><span><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx17\">(C++17)</span></span></span></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  spherical Bessel functions (of the first kind) <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(function)</span> </td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/special_functions/sph_legendre\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>sph_legendre</span><span>sph_legendref</span><span>sph_legendrel</span></span></a></div><div><span class=\"t-lines\"><span><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx17\">(C++17)</span></span><span><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx17\">(C++17)</span></span><span><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx17\">(C++17)</span></span></span></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  spherical associated Legendre functions <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(function)</span> </td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/special_functions/sph_neumann\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>sph_neumann</span><span>sph_neumannf</span><span>sph_neumannl</span></span></a></div><div><span class=\"t-lines\"><span><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx17\">(C++17)</span></span><span><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx17\">(C++17)</span></span><span><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx17\">(C++17)</span></span></span></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  spherical Neumann functions <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(function)</span> </td></tr>\n</table>\n<h3 id=\"Notes\">Notes</h3>\n<p>The <span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw4\">float</span></span> and <span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw4\">long</span> <span class=\"kw4\">double</span></span> overloads for math special functions without the \"<code>f</code>\" or \"<code>l</code>\" suffix are present in the final draft of ISO/IEC 29124:2010 (<a class=\"external text\" href=\"https://wg21.link/N3060\" data-external=\"1\">N3060</a>), but absent in the published C++17/20 standard (see <a class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cplusplus.github.io/LWG/issue3234\" data-external=\"1\">LWG issue 3234</a>). These overloads were not provided by MSVC STL until VS 2022 17.3.\n</p><p>These functions are unrelated to <a href=\"/w/cpp/language/member_functions#Special_member_functions\">special member functions</a> of class types.\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable ftm-begin ftm-has-value\">\n<tr>\n<th><a href=\"/w/cpp/utility/feature_test\">Feature-test</a> macro</th>\n<th><abbr>Value</abbr></th>\n<th><abbr>Std</abbr></th>\n<th>Feature\n</th></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a href=\"/w/cpp/feature_test#cpp_lib_math_special_functions\"><code>__cpp_lib_math_special_functions</code></a></td>\n<td><a href=\"/w/cpp/compiler_support/17#cpp_lib_math_special_functions_201603L\"><code>201603L</code></a></td>\n<td><span class=\"t-mark\">(C++17)</span></td>\n<td><a href=\"#\">Mathematical special functions</a>\n</td></tr></table>\n<h3 id=\"Defect_reports\">Defect reports</h3>\n<p>The following behavior-changing defect reports were applied retroactively to previously published C++ standards.\n</p>\n<table class=\"dsctable\">\n<tr>\n<th>DR\n</th>\n<th>Applied to\n</th>\n<th>Behavior as published\n</th>\n<th>Correct behavior\n</th></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cplusplus.github.io/LWG/issue3234\" data-external=\"1\">LWG 3234</a><br>(<a class=\"external text\" href=\"https://wg21.link/P1467R9\" data-external=\"1\">P1467R9</a>)\n</td>\n<td>C++17\n</td>\n<td>additional overloads for math special functions were missing\n</td>\n<td>these overloads are required\n</td></tr></table>\n<h3 id=\"References\">References</h3>\n<div class=\"t-ref-std-c++23\">\n<ul><li> C++23 standard (ISO/IEC 14882:2024): \n</li></ul>\n<dl><dd><ul><li> 28.7.6 Mathematical special functions [sf.cmath] \n</li></ul>\n</dd></dl>\n</div>\n<div class=\"t-ref-std-c++20\">\n<ul><li> C++20 standard (ISO/IEC 14882:2020): \n</li></ul>\n<dl><dd><ul><li> 26.8.6 Mathematical special functions [sf.cmath] \n</li></ul>\n</dd></dl>\n</div>\n<div class=\"t-ref-std-c++17\">\n<ul><li> C++17 standard (ISO/IEC 14882:2017): \n</li></ul>\n<dl><dd><ul><li> 29.9.5 Mathematical special functions [sf.cmath] \n</li></ul>\n</dd></dl>\n</div>","headings":[{"depth":3,"text":"Functions","id":"Functions"},{"depth":3,"text":"Notes","id":"Notes"},{"depth":3,"text":"Defect reports","id":"Defect_reports"},{"depth":3,"text":"References","id":"References"}],"breadcrumbs":[{"path":"","title":"C++ reference"},{"path":"numeric","title":"Numerics library"}],"children":[{"path":"numeric/special_functions/assoc_laguerre","title":"std::assoc_laguerre, std::assoc_laguerref, std::assoc_laguerrel"},{"path":"numeric/special_functions/assoc_legendre","title":"std::assoc_legendre, std::assoc_legendref, std::assoc_legendrel"},{"path":"numeric/special_functions/beta","title":"std::beta, std::betaf, std::betal"},{"path":"numeric/special_functions/comp_ellint_1","title":"std::comp_ellint_1, std::comp_ellint_1f, std::comp_ellint_1l"},{"path":"numeric/special_functions/comp_ellint_2","title":"std::comp_ellint_2, std::comp_ellint_2f, std::comp_ellint_2l"},{"path":"numeric/special_functions/comp_ellint_3","title":"std::comp_ellint_3, std::comp_ellint_3f, std::comp_ellint_3l"},{"path":"numeric/special_functions/cyl_bessel_i","title":"std::cyl_bessel_i, std::cyl_bessel_if, std::cyl_bessel_il"},{"path":"numeric/special_functions/cyl_bessel_j","title":"std::cyl_bessel_j, std::cyl_bessel_jf, std::cyl_bessel_jl"},{"path":"numeric/special_functions/cyl_bessel_k","title":"std::cyl_bessel_k, std::cyl_bessel_kf, std::cyl_bessel_kl"},{"path":"numeric/special_functions/cyl_neumann","title":"std::cyl_neumann, std::cyl_neumannf, std::cyl_neumannl"},{"path":"numeric/special_functions/ellint_1","title":"std::ellint_1, std::ellint_1f, std::e